":[{"type":"text","text":"The reason for this API using a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ResultHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than returning values directly,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is that thanks to this approach it can avoid any existential boxing, and can serve the most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"latency sensitive-use-cases."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Throws","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the target location, invocation argument decoding, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"some other mismatch between them happens. In general, this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method is allowed to throw in any situation that might otherwise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"result in an illegal or unexpected invocation being performed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["    Throws ``ExecuteDistributedTargetMissingAccessorError`` if the `target`","    does not resolve to a valid distributed function accessor, i.e. the","    call identifier is incorrect, corrupted, or simply not present in this process."]}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/LocalTestingDistributedActorSystem\/executeDistributedTarget(on:target:invocationDecoder:handler:)"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/distributed\/localtestingdistributedactorsystem\/executedistributedtarget(on:target:invocationdecoder:handler:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Prepare and execute a call to the distributed function identified by the passed arguments,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the passed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actor"},{"type":"text","text":", and collect its results using the "},{"type":"cod